1
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,400
The storm rises

2
00:02:35,319 --> 00:02:36,199
on the peak.

3
00:02:36,639 --> 00:02:37,759
The traveler shall not return.

4
00:02:38,759 --> 00:02:39,960
A barren womb

5
00:02:40,879 --> 00:02:42,240
that bears no fruit.

6
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:43,879
The omen is dark.

7
00:02:44,599 --> 00:02:45,159
No fruit?

8
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:45,960
Holy One,

9
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,039
speak plainly.

10
00:02:47,439 --> 00:02:48,439
My lord and I

11
00:02:48,599 --> 00:02:50,120
yearn for an heir.

12
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,680
We have sought

13
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:52,879
every healer,

14
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:54,719
yet our cradle remains empty.

15
00:02:54,879 --> 00:02:57,039
Do not despair, My Lady.

16
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:58,879
A son is written

17
00:02:59,159 --> 00:03:01,280
in Lord Gu's fate.

18
00:03:01,759 --> 00:03:02,439
Though

19
00:03:03,439 --> 00:03:04,759
his life-spark burns dim.

20
00:03:05,039 --> 00:03:06,280
Yet, destiny

21
00:03:07,159 --> 00:03:09,360
is not set in stone.

22
00:03:10,159 --> 00:03:10,919
With pious deeds

23
00:03:10,919 --> 00:03:13,159
and charity,

24
00:03:13,240 --> 00:03:15,639
the gods may relent.

25
00:03:16,080 --> 00:03:16,840
Praise the gods!

26
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,199
My love,

27
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,159
we shall have our heir!

28
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:26,599
Holy One,

29
00:03:27,319 --> 00:03:28,439
from this day forth,

30
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,000
on every new and full moon,

31
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:31,639
I shall fast

32
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:32,719
and pray

33
00:03:33,199 --> 00:03:34,800
within

34
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:35,960
these walls.

35
00:03:36,439 --> 00:03:37,439
May the gods

36
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:39,159
grant our house

37
00:03:39,479 --> 00:03:40,400
an heir.

38
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:41,719
Your devotion

39
00:03:42,199 --> 00:03:43,879
shall move the heavens.

40
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:47,039
May the gods watch over you!

41
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:55,919
[Merciful gods,]

42
00:03:56,479 --> 00:03:57,479
[grand me an heir, ]

43
00:03:58,199 --> 00:03:59,560
[and I shall pledge my life]

44
00:04:00,199 --> 00:04:01,120
[in return.]

45
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:06,199
Zhishu left in such haste.

46
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,400
So secretive.

47
00:04:08,879 --> 00:04:10,400
What if he is

48
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:11,560
in peril?

49
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:12,800
Fret not, fair sister.

50
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:14,360
He never

51
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,680
deprives himself

52
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,079
of comfort.

53
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:19,279
Besides, he is a master of the sword.

54
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,480
No harm shall find him.

55
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,240
We always knelt here as three,

56
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,560
praying for our parents.

57
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,439
I used to find his chatter tiresome.

58
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:28,600
Now, his absence

59
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:30,040
leaves a cold silence.

60
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:31,839
When will he return?

61
00:04:33,079 --> 00:04:34,600
He thinks himself

62
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,560
cast aside.

63
00:04:36,639 --> 00:04:37,839
Yet he's barely gone,

64
00:04:38,199 --> 00:04:39,680
and the house feels empty.

65
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,600
Catch me!

66
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:44,319
Master. My Lady.

67
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,519
Peace be with you.

68
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:46,120
Zhili.

69
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:48,199
Your seat was empty yesterday.

70
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:50,000
What befell you?

71
00:04:50,759 --> 00:04:51,879
A slight fever,

72
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:52,959
Master.

73
00:04:53,240 --> 00:04:54,160
Nothing more.

74
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,199
Did the healer tend to you?

75
00:04:55,279 --> 00:04:55,959
My Lord,

76
00:04:56,920 --> 00:04:57,560
My Lady.

77
00:04:58,079 --> 00:05:00,000
Do you seek the gods' grace today?

78
00:05:00,519 --> 00:05:02,519
We pray for an heir.

79
00:05:02,879 --> 00:05:04,720
To secure

80
00:05:05,079 --> 00:05:06,040
the Gus' bloodline.

81
00:05:06,879 --> 00:05:08,639
May your prayers

82
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:09,959
be answered.

83
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:11,519
- Dear sister!
- Careful!

84
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:13,879
Keep up!

85
00:05:14,079 --> 00:05:14,879
Almost there!

86
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:16,040
Are you bruised?

87
00:05:17,439 --> 00:05:18,120
I am well.

88
00:05:22,079 --> 00:05:24,360
How fiercely protective.

89
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:25,680
My love,

90
00:05:25,879 --> 00:05:26,639
behold,

91
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:29,199
what a perfect match.

92
00:05:29,399 --> 00:05:30,279
They bear no resemblance

93
00:05:30,279 --> 00:05:31,160
to siblings.

94
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,560
We share no blood.

95
00:05:33,439 --> 00:05:34,000
Fair sister,

96
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,040
come.

97
00:05:35,399 --> 00:05:36,759
The altar awaits.

98
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,160
We must

99
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,480
bid you farewell.

100
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,639
You made

101
00:05:52,759 --> 00:05:53,879
a fool of yourself.

102
00:05:54,199 --> 00:05:54,600
It was but

103
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:55,680
a minor stumble.

104
00:05:55,879 --> 00:05:57,000
Yet you trembled like a leaf.

105
00:05:59,079 --> 00:05:59,759
Look at them.

106
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,199
Green and fair,

107
00:06:01,199 --> 00:06:02,160
bound by Venus herself.

108
00:06:02,399 --> 00:06:03,279
You are

109
00:06:03,519 --> 00:06:04,519
a graying man.

110
00:06:04,759 --> 00:06:06,079
Do not let lust

111
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:07,439
rot your reputation!

112
00:06:09,439 --> 00:06:10,319
This is a holy place.

113
00:06:10,879 --> 00:06:12,079
Silence your wicked tongue.

114
00:06:12,759 --> 00:06:14,439
Before the gods,

115
00:06:15,040 --> 00:06:16,319
you should fear

116
00:06:16,639 --> 00:06:17,959
your own dark thoughts!

117
00:06:19,879 --> 00:06:20,600
Your eyes...

118
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:23,920
they held the same fire they did

119
00:06:25,079 --> 00:06:26,319
when you first

120
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:27,319
gazed upon me...

121
00:06:27,319 --> 00:06:28,000
Insolence!

122
00:06:29,279 --> 00:06:30,800
Silence your slander!

123
00:07:26,759 --> 00:07:28,519
Have you waited long, Your Majesty?

124
00:07:29,839 --> 00:07:30,800
I have only just arrived.

125
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:48,399
The tea is perfectly brewed.

126
00:07:49,199 --> 00:07:50,759
Sit,

127
00:07:51,199 --> 00:07:52,040
warm yourself.

128
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,759
You are

129
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:20,959
usually so fierce.

130
00:08:21,480 --> 00:08:22,959
Why does your heart flutter so tonight?

131
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,240
The noodles will grow cold.

132
00:08:25,879 --> 00:08:26,959
Pray, taste them.

133
00:08:39,639 --> 00:08:42,039
The royal kitchens boast

134
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:43,039
the finest delicacies,

135
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:45,440
yet this lamb broth

136
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,399
warms my soul far better.

137
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,639
Did no other dish

138
00:08:51,879 --> 00:08:53,720
tempt your palate,

139
00:08:54,039 --> 00:08:55,440
Your Majesty?

140
00:08:57,399 --> 00:09:00,240
Are you trying to unravel me?

141
00:09:01,320 --> 00:09:03,519
My life is an open book to you.

142
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:07,120
I shall read a page of yours,

143
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,039
Your Majesty.

144
00:09:16,080 --> 00:09:17,159
When I

145
00:09:17,879 --> 00:09:19,120
was a lad,

146
00:09:19,480 --> 00:09:20,799
my mother made

147
00:09:22,919 --> 00:09:24,519
sweet pastries.

148
00:09:25,759 --> 00:09:26,840
When she passed,

149
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,240
I gorged myself

150
00:09:28,799 --> 00:09:29,759
on twelve chests of it,

151
00:09:30,159 --> 00:09:32,000
weeping until

152
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,279
I spat blood.

153
00:09:33,519 --> 00:09:34,360
Since then,

154
00:09:35,519 --> 00:09:37,279
food has held no joy

155
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,080
for me.

156
00:09:39,639 --> 00:09:41,919
We hunger for

157
00:09:42,919 --> 00:09:44,039
the hands

158
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,559
that fed us.

159
00:09:47,279 --> 00:09:49,320
When I see apricot cake,

160
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,000
I remember Xiang.

161
00:09:55,639 --> 00:09:56,639
You brought flavor

162
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,480
back to my life.

163
00:09:59,639 --> 00:10:00,519
Think of me

164
00:10:01,519 --> 00:10:02,759
when you taste this.

165
00:10:17,679 --> 00:10:18,480
Snow!

166
00:10:33,679 --> 00:10:35,120
I never saw snow in Shazhou.

167
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:37,559
Wishes made on the first snow

168
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:39,240
are granted by the gods.

169
00:10:40,519 --> 00:10:42,600
I fear I have missed it.

170
00:10:45,519 --> 00:10:47,000
Why petition the gods?

171
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,120
A prayer to me may be pragmatic.

172
00:10:53,320 --> 00:10:54,279
Then I pray for

173
00:10:54,639 --> 00:10:55,840
the downfall of Ling Yunfei,

174
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,600
the ruin of his Tiger Roar bandits,

175
00:10:57,919 --> 00:11:00,519
and eternal peace for our lands.

176
00:11:06,519 --> 00:11:07,600
And what does the Crown pray for?

177
00:11:13,559 --> 00:11:15,200
By the heavens, this is scandalous!

178
00:11:15,559 --> 00:11:16,080
They...

179
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:19,399
Hush! Shall we summon the heralds

180
00:11:19,559 --> 00:11:20,919
and blow the trumpets too?

181
00:11:23,039 --> 00:11:24,639
A royal tryst?

182
00:11:24,840 --> 00:11:26,440
In the gardens?

183
00:11:26,639 --> 00:11:27,320
Witching the Crown

184
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:28,320
is a death sentence!

185
00:11:28,559 --> 00:11:30,320
They will tear her limb from limb!

186
00:11:30,320 --> 00:11:31,399
Watch your tongue!

187
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,440
They are debating the affairs

188
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,039
of the realm.

189
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:34,559
Affairs

190
00:11:34,559 --> 00:11:35,840
of the realm?

191
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:37,879
Feeding him like

192
00:11:38,159 --> 00:11:39,679
a tavern maid?

193
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,200
It is a disgrace!

194
00:11:41,399 --> 00:11:42,600
I shall intervene before honor dies!

195
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:47,159
Your prayers shall be granted.

196
00:11:49,080 --> 00:11:49,960
May

197
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:51,399
the winter never

198
00:11:52,399 --> 00:11:53,759
find me without companionship.

199
00:12:00,480 --> 00:12:01,440
We are both

200
00:12:01,440 --> 00:12:02,399
kinless.

201
00:12:03,879 --> 00:12:05,480
Adored by millions,

202
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,279
yet you spend the feast nights

203
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,080
in solitude.

204
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:12,120
I pray

205
00:12:13,399 --> 00:12:14,399
your hall

206
00:12:14,799 --> 00:12:16,000
is never

207
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:18,320
cold

208
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,720
again.

209
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,200
When the spring blooms,

210
00:12:28,879 --> 00:12:30,600
shall we cast our prayers upon the waters?

211
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,080
I pledge it.

212
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:43,639
Disgraceful!

213
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,120
A sovereign whoring with his own minister?

214
00:12:48,440 --> 00:12:49,799
He spits on the laws of the realm!

215
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:50,799
I knew

216
00:12:50,799 --> 00:12:51,440
that baseborn girl

217
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:53,039
was poison!

218
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:55,080
The whole realm

219
00:12:55,759 --> 00:12:57,120
whispers of his shame!

220
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,960
How have you failed your watch?!

221
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,559
The girl has a tragic past.

222
00:13:01,720 --> 00:13:02,720
His Majesty snatched her

223
00:13:02,720 --> 00:13:03,919
from the slavers.

224
00:13:03,919 --> 00:13:05,840
It is but a lingering pity.

225
00:13:05,840 --> 00:13:06,960
The whispers in the taverns

226
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:08,320
are lies!

227
00:13:08,440 --> 00:13:10,120
He is now

228
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:10,919
the laughingstock

229
00:13:10,919 --> 00:13:12,480
of the lowborn!

230
00:13:12,519 --> 00:13:14,120
The Crown's honor is bled dry!

231
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,480
He reads the

232
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,600
ancient decrees

233
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,159
every dawn.

234
00:13:19,720 --> 00:13:22,240
Surely His Majesty knows his bounds.

235
00:13:22,399 --> 00:13:23,840
Yet his chambers

236
00:13:24,159 --> 00:13:25,320
remain empty!

237
00:13:25,639 --> 00:13:26,919
No son to secure the succession!

238
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:29,200
The throne cannot stand without an heir!

239
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:31,159
I have sweated blood over this.

240
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:32,919
When the

241
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,240
noble maidens danced,

242
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,639
his wrath nearly

243
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:37,159
saw me

244
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:39,039
executed!

245
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,559
An heir would

246
00:13:44,559 --> 00:13:47,120
bind his wandering heart.

247
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:49,360
My Lord,

248
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:50,519
what is your counsel?

249
00:14:01,919 --> 00:14:03,000
My love,

250
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,039
the whispers of the Crown and Lady Meng

251
00:14:06,240 --> 00:14:07,879
grow louder by the day.

252
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,039
I've gazed upon her

253
00:14:10,159 --> 00:14:11,759
at feasts.

254
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:14,399
She is poised and dignified,

255
00:14:15,159 --> 00:14:17,440
not the siren they paint her

256
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:18,360
to be.

257
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,360
If the Crown

258
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:21,759
is smitten,

259
00:14:21,919 --> 00:14:23,440
I cannot blame him.

260
00:14:25,559 --> 00:14:27,879
A sovereign bedding his minister

261
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:29,399
is a scandal.

262
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,080
We shall

263
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:33,480
have Wen Ruomei sent to the palace.

264
00:14:34,679 --> 00:14:35,720
That shall extinguish

265
00:14:36,039 --> 00:14:37,799
Meng's hopes.

266
00:14:38,879 --> 00:14:39,919
That maiden

267
00:14:40,279 --> 00:14:41,840
is dull-witted.

268
00:14:42,159 --> 00:14:44,159
She lacks the grace to wear a crown!

269
00:14:44,799 --> 00:14:46,000
Words of a simple mind!

270
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:47,759
It is vital we sever

271
00:14:47,759 --> 00:14:49,559
the Crown's attachment

272
00:14:49,759 --> 00:14:51,240
to Meng Tinghui!

273
00:14:52,159 --> 00:14:53,399
You bury yourself

274
00:14:53,399 --> 00:14:55,759
in statecraft,

275
00:14:55,799 --> 00:14:57,320
yet you ignore our own house.

276
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,320
Our son is of age.

277
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:01,240
You should find him

278
00:15:01,279 --> 00:15:02,559
a lady

279
00:15:02,679 --> 00:15:04,519
of high birth.

280
00:15:06,960 --> 00:15:08,120
If you and the lad

281
00:15:08,480 --> 00:15:09,840
have chosen a maiden,

282
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:11,360
name her.

283
00:15:11,559 --> 00:15:12,600
No house in the realm

284
00:15:12,919 --> 00:15:15,159
would dare refuse us.

285
00:15:15,679 --> 00:15:16,519
Father!

286
00:15:16,559 --> 00:15:17,240
Mother!

287
00:15:18,399 --> 00:15:19,399
Fetch the finest matchmakers

288
00:15:19,399 --> 00:15:20,360
in the realm!

289
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,480
I have found

290
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:23,080
the lady of my heart!

291
00:15:24,960 --> 00:15:26,639
Listen to him!

292
00:15:26,799 --> 00:15:28,039
Our little bird is ready to

293
00:15:28,039 --> 00:15:28,879
build his nest!

294
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:29,799
Tell us,

295
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:31,679
who is she?

296
00:15:33,039 --> 00:15:34,000
She is

297
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:34,639
no

298
00:15:34,639 --> 00:15:36,320
mere mortal!

299
00:15:36,759 --> 00:15:39,840
She is a moon-goddess

300
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:41,840
fallen to earth!

301
00:15:42,039 --> 00:15:44,759
A vision of peerless grace!

302
00:15:44,799 --> 00:15:46,200
Her every breath is music...

303
00:15:47,159 --> 00:15:49,080
What a poet we have raised!

304
00:15:49,279 --> 00:15:50,039
Pray tell,

305
00:15:50,039 --> 00:15:51,399
